1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:06,320
<i>Junjai is the girl you've been seeing</i>
<i>in your dreams, isn't she?</i>

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,240
<i>Since I met her,</i>

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,680
<i>I haven't been able</i>
<i>to stop thinking about her.</i>

4
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:17,280
From now on,
Junjai is Toxxxxin's fifth member.

5
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:21,120
<i>If you mess with her, you mess with us.</i>

6
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:27,440
Do I really get to be
this close to you every day?

7
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:46,840
<i>Have you ever felt like</i>
<i>you were half asleep and half awake?</i>

8
00:00:58,280 --> 00:00:59,760
Go ahead and eat, Junjai.

9
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:03,000
- I've got your breakfast ready.
- Okay.

10
00:01:17,480 --> 00:01:20,320
Am I going to have to braid your hair
until you're in college?

11
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:25,200
Thanks, Auntie In.

12
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:37,960
I'm sorry I told her
you were part of our group.

13
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:45,080
But until we're sure
no one's going to bully you anymore,

14
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:50,720
just think of yourself
as the fifth member of Toxxxxin.

15
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:57,240
Auntie In?

16
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:05,520
If I told you I'd joined
the school's most popular group,

17
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:06,720
would you believe me?

18
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,000
What kind of question is that?

19
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,280
Of course I would.

20
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,920
My niece is gorgeous.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,960
You've got an amazing figure.

22
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,960
What's so gorgeous about me?

23
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:22,840
You're the only one who ever says that.

24
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:28,320
<i>Suddenly, I feel like I'm waking up,</i>
<i>yet somehow still dreaming.</i>

25
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:33,640
<i>No matter how hard I try</i>
<i>to live my life as usual,</i>

26
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,440
<i>sometimes, what's in front of me</i>
<i>feels strangely unreal.</i>

27
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:54,960
<i>And sometimes,</i>
<i>it feels so real it scares me.</i>

28
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:59,360
Full team!
Took you long enough, kiddo.

29
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,640
We've got so much to talk about.

30
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,680
Let's hurry back to our room.

31
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,080
Huh?

32
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,240
Why so confused?

33
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:12,120
We promised, remember?

34
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:16,440
Are you going to wait until school's over?

35
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,360
Come on, let's go!

36
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,040
<i>If all of this really is just a dream,</i>

37
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:30,120
<i>then I'll make the most of</i>
<i>this short dream!</i>

38
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:03,720
Okay, we don't have much time
before the bell,

39
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,120
so let's get straight to it.

40
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:10,600
We've already come up with a plan
to stop you from getting bullied.

41
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:14,040
Do you know the first thing you need?

42
00:04:16,160 --> 00:04:17,480
It's…?

43
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:19,720
It's…?

44
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,959
A self-defense weapon?

45
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,200
I mean, she's not wrong.

46
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:27,840
Beauty, dear.

47
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:33,640
You need to feel confident, and looking
good is the easiest way to get there.

48
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:39,200
So your clothes, your hair, your makeup,
and this whole look of yours

49
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,720
are getting a complete makeover.

50
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:45,280
Hey, I'll start with her nails today.

51
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,800
Just enough, not too much.

52
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:51,160
But wouldn't that break school rules?

53
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:01,360
We'll deal with that later.

54
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,240
We've got our ways.

55
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,680
You should've told her first.

56
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,280
You scared her. See?

57
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:10,880
Go on. Help with her hair.

58
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,520
What color should we use?

59
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:20,320
You guys are nothing like I imagined.

60
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,680
How so?

61
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:29,360
I thought you kept to yourselves,

62
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:34,520
didn't hang out with anyone,
and seemed cold.

63
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:37,480
But actually,

64
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:42,640
you're really sweet and so down-to-earth.

65
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:49,000
Aww, you are so cute.

66
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:51,720
You're so adorable.

67
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,400
Can I keep her at home?

68
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:56,360
Hey, stop talking nonsense.
We're running out of time.

69
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:00,440
- Shit, you're right.
- Shit.

70
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,880
Let me take your measurements first, okay?

71
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,440
I'll leave this to you.

72
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,320
What?

73
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:11,960
We're busy over here.

74
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:12,960
Go.

75
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:13,880
Be careful.

76
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:16,040
Nails!

77
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,240
Why are you covering your face?

78
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,880
Well, I don't really like my face.

79
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:59,080
If you don't like it, who will?

80
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:10,400
The important thing is
learning to love yourself first.

81
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,120
You know that?

82
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:16,760
You're so pretty,

83
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,920
and you've got a great figure.

84
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:28,720
You know, you sound just like my aunt.

85
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
What?

86
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,960
Are you saying I'm old?

87
00:07:34,960 --> 00:07:37,480
No! I meant…

88
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,680
- I didn't mean it like that.
- Then what did you mean?

89
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,480
- Nothing like that.
- So what did you mean?

90
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:46,480
Well, I just meant…

91
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,960
Hey, we've got three minutes left.

92
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:52,400
You're so good at ruining the mood!

93
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:55,720
Come on, sweetie. Let's finish
getting you dressed. Come on.

94
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,040
Your nails.

95
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,080
Gale, come help me iron this.

96
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:05,120
WE'VE CHANGED YOUR DESK.

97
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:13,840
Junjai, what did you do?

98
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:15,440
Your hairstyle is insanely amazing.

99
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,680
Thanks.

100
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:22,000
I look weird, don't I?

101
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,080
Weird? You look like an Asian supermodel.

102
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,760
Don't tell me the Toxxxxin girls
gave you a makeover!?

103
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:30,680
Tell us about it!

104
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,080
IS SHE A NEW STUDENT???

105
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,600
- #WHAT DID JJ DO?
- YES???

106
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,280
- TOXXXXXIN'S FIFTH MEMBER
- SHE'S FABBIE.

107
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,680
- I ALMOST COULDN'T RECOGNIZE HER.
- FROM ZERO TO SUPERSTAR.

108
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:43,320
Guys, our little puppy
is getting complimented!

109
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,440
Her beauty aura is on its way.

110
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,200
Look.

111
00:09:59,280 --> 00:10:00,400
Maybe not yet.

112
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:06,000
Should we go for it now?

113
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:10,000
Let's do it.

114
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,200
Okay, the next step is

115
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,640
to change how you present yourself online.

116
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,920
Start a new account and make it private.

117
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Pretty, poised, and a little mysterious.

118
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,880
You don't have to force it, though.

119
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:27,160
Just be yourself.
That's the best thing you can do.

120
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:32,920
But if I act the same,
won't everything stay the same?

121
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,320
No.

122
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:39,680
You get bullied because
people see you as beneath them.

123
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,280
It's like they've stuck a label on you.

124
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:44,120
We're just peeling it off.

125
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:47,560
If you're still uncomfortable,

126
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,040
you can play a little hard to get.

127
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:57,440
And that wraps up phase one.

128
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,720
What a shame, though.

129
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,920
I wish we could give her a fabulous debut.

130
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,840
Like a grand opening!

131
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:08,240
Don't. If we force it,
it'll look like we're trying too hard.

132
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:11,640
See you in class. I'm going up for a nap.

133
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:15,640
Come on. You've barely helped
since she got here.

134
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:17,320
This isn't my thing.

135
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:19,000
Do whatever you want.

136
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:28,760
Gale.

137
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:32,280
We need to make a poster
to promote Sports Day.

138
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:35,440
We were hoping an athlete
could model for us.

139
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,320
Ask someone else.

140
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:41,440
I don't think I'm the right fit.

141
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:44,760
Aww, but you're the perfect choice
when it comes to sports.

142
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,400
You're also gorgeous.

143
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,760
If you modeled for us,
the poster would look amazing.

144
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,720
- Please?
- Please, please, please?

145
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:59,200
ACTUALLY, JUNJAI HAS
THE LOOK OF A MODEL.

146
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,560
- Please, Gale.
- Just follow my lead.

147
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:02,680
Let's put it this way.

148
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:05,120
She might be shy to shoot alone.

149
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:07,400
We'll help.

150
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:14,040
But can we tweak the concept a little?

151
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:24,600
Uncle Jes!

152
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:28,160
Do you have any outfits we could borrow?!

153
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,360
What?!

154
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:49,200
That's fab. So professional!

155
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,040
This is right up your alley, huh?

156
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,440
You guys owe me a meal.

157
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,760
<i>Okay, next up are the pair shots.</i>

158
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,080
Hey, does this look okay?

159
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,280
Yeah. Go for it!

160
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:10,400
Gale, help her out, please.

161
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,680
Okay, pose, please.

162
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:20,760
Stunning. Keep going.

163
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,520
Gorgeous.

164
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:30,040
When you hold a racket,

165
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,320
put this hand here.

166
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,200
Then support it with this hand.

167
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:43,400
Thank you.

168
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,160
Let's get this over with

169
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,160
so I can leave already.

170
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,600
Keep posing.

171
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:52,040
Should we ship them?

172
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,000
Stop!

173
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:56,800
Still, this is nice.

174
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:01,120
Now that's more like a grand opening.

175
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,560
- SLAY!!!
- ROGER THAT!

176
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,320
- GAY PANIC! GALE'S SUPER FABULOUS.
- JUNJAI'S POSTER IS FAB TOO.

177
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,520
YOUR BEST ENERGY!

178
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,640
YEAH. SHE SLAYS.

179
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,680
I'M DYING.

180
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:16,520
- I SHIP THEM.
- JJ = JUST JAW-DROPPING!

181
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,720
- THE CHEMISTRY!
- THAT SLAPS!

182
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:53,360
Something like this takes time, you know?

183
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:54,960
So just don't care.

184
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:03,280
There's one last thing you need to do.

185
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,600
This one's going to be tough.

186
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,200
You'll have to do it on your own.

187
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:20,960
As a math scholarship student,

188
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:23,440
you must know about next week's
Athena Mathematics competition.

189
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,240
Our school is hosting this year.

190
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,120
Students from other schools
will be coming here.

191
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,680
If you win a gold medal,

192
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,920
your standing here will change overnight.

193
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,280
You've got the looks.

194
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,880
Now you just need to prove your brains.

195
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:40,880
Once you bring the school some glory,
everything will get much easier.

196
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:46,840
But I've never entered
a competition this big before.

197
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,080
You can do it.

198
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:49,720
Believe in yourself.

199
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,840
Okay. I'll give it a try.

200
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:58,760
Good.

201
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:01,560
Leave the application paperwork to us.
We'll take care of it.

202
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:05,040
Here are the papers from previous years.

203
00:16:05,120 --> 00:16:07,360
We got them from the documents room.

204
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,600
Don't let these get out.

205
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,960
But aren't students banned
from going in there?

206
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,240
They can't stop Gale.

207
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:20,280
But don't worry.

208
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,840
We only took papers from previous years.

209
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,560
Our school's so weird.

210
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:26,400
Other schools let students
look at past papers.

211
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:28,280
Why keep them under wraps?

212
00:16:28,360 --> 00:16:31,160
This year's papers are
in there too, right?

213
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:35,160
Hey, taking those would be cheating.

214
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:43,000
Okay, I've got other things to do.

215
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,160
I need to take the sulky girl to lunch.

216
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:48,760
I'll go get your things, then.

217
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:52,240
I'll leave her to you, Tutor Chelsea.

218
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:53,520
You can do it!

219
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:02,400
Pretty cool, huh?

220
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:05,800
In a weird way, though.

221
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:11,079
The more I get to know you,

222
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:14,200
the more amazing I think you all are.

223
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:16,280
You're all so cool.

224
00:17:17,880 --> 00:17:19,200
It feels like a dream.

225
00:17:20,319 --> 00:17:21,319
What dream?

226
00:17:22,599 --> 00:17:23,560
Seriously.

227
00:17:24,839 --> 00:17:26,520
I still don't understand

228
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:30,160
why you're helping someone like me.

229
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,880
That's a secret.

230
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,080
Let me put it this way.

231
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:49,600
Actually, we're all different
in lots of ways,

232
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,440
like why we keep our accounts private.

233
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,560
Do you want to know why?

234
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,880
Do you know this actress?

235
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,360
Oh, I've seen her.

236
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:12,840
She used to play leading roles,

237
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:15,320
then started a page
when she had a kid, right?

238
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,200
She was really popular for a while.

239
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,080
Her kid was so cute.

240
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,520
That's my mom.

241
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:29,840
<i>She's been trying to make me famous</i>
<i>since I was little.</i>

242
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,920
<i>Everything in my life was work.</i>

243
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,080
<i>Everything was for show.</i>

244
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,400
<i>Footprints were everywhere.</i>

245
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,400
I got so sick of it.

246
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:39,080
Eventually, I had to talk it out with her.

247
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,560
I told her I wanted to stop.
I needed a detox.

248
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,120
Seriously?

249
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,200
As for Meimei…

250
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,560
<i>Nothing much.</i>

251
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:51,360
<i>Her family's just a typical rich family.</i>
<i>They run a used-car dealership.</i>

252
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:56,400
<i>The problem is, her family's taste</i>
<i>is kind of embarrassing.</i>

253
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:59,480
<i>Meimei always says</i>
<i>her family doesn't just deal in cars.</i>

254
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,080
They deal in embarrassment too.

255
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,080
As for Gale,

256
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,920
<i>she's really gifted at arts,</i>

257
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:11,080
<i>but she comes from</i>
<i>a family of doctors,</i>

258
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:12,880
<i>so they aren't too keen on it.</i>

259
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,720
<i>She started pushing back.</i>

260
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,720
<i>Things are better now, though.</i>

261
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,680
Her family's starting to accept it.

262
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:24,280
That's why we stay off social media.

263
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:25,880
Nothing dramatic.

264
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,760
We've all just got our own silly reasons.

265
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,040
How about…?

266
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:39,240
But Aidao is different.

267
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:46,160
<i>Her dad's a famous politician.</i>

268
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,760
Ouch.

269
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,480
<i>With a perfect public image.</i>

270
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,520
<i>But at the same time,</i>

271
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:57,000
<i>he's also a high-ranking military officer</i>
<i>who raises his children with an iron fist.</i>

272
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,440
<i>Whenever they make a mistake,</i>

273
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:01,880
<i>the result is violence.</i>

274
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,800
<i>To us,</i>

275
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:08,280
Aidao's life is like a cage.

276
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:14,440
And we hope so damn much
that one day she'll break free.

277
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:20,680
Why are you telling me all this?

278
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:24,280
That's because, honestly,

279
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:26,920
Aidao wants to help you.

280
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,760
But we want to help Aidao.

281
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:38,480
And our intuition tells us that
if we keep helping you,

282
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:42,240
something will change someday.

283
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:46,200
Don't underestimate our intuition.

284
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,640
It's pretty powerful.

285
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:51,280
So make sure you really thank Aidao.

286
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,520
Her own life's hard enough,

287
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,000
but she still wants to help you.

288
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:56,400
Look.

289
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:59,240
She put together
all these casual outfits for you,

290
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,200
so you can look good on other days too.

291
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:04,720
And these are tons of skincare products.

292
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:06,040
Make sure you use them.

293
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:18,960
DON'T FORGET TO LIKE YOURSELF TOO.

294
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,800
Keep fighting, Junjai.

295
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,840
Aidao's really rooting for you.

296
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:32,600
Okay, let's start studying.

297
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:34,120
We've spent way too long gossiping.

298
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,880
- Come on.
- Put it away already.

299
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,080
Thank you.

300
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,160
This one, okay?

301
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:41,200
This one.

302
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:40,600
DON'T FORGET TO LIKE YOURSELF TOO.

303
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:51,640
CUZ I'M STARTING TO TOO.

304
00:23:11,920 --> 00:23:15,600
HOW TO LOOK BEAUTIFUL
FROM MORNING TILL BEDTIME

305
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:17,080
LAUNDRY

306
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,400
Come here.
Your hair's getting in your food.

307
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:42,200
Well…

308
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:43,360
But you know,

309
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:47,600
I love braiding your hair, Junjai.

310
00:24:49,520 --> 00:24:51,880
Your hair looks beautiful.

311
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:54,040
Braids really suit you.

312
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:06,960
YOU DON'T BELONG IN TOXXXXIN!

313
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:14,520
Gotcha.

314
00:25:14,600 --> 00:25:17,680
You act like you don't care,
but you're worried about her, right?

315
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:21,680
I just wanted to check how she's doing.

316
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:23,560
Sure. Playing it cool, huh?

317
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:27,360
You've actually opened up to her.
I can tell.

318
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:31,880
Honestly, I haven't.

319
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:35,640
We've only known her for a few days.

320
00:25:36,360 --> 00:25:39,840
Isn't it too soon to trust her?

321
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:44,240
Aren't you putting up
too many walls this time?

322
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,480
I'm not putting up walls.

323
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:49,440
You guys realize

324
00:25:50,280 --> 00:25:53,280
just how hard you're pushing her
by doing this, right?

325
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:07,080
I SAW TOXXXXIN'S FIFTH MEMBER.

326
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,880
BUS STOP

327
00:26:40,320 --> 00:26:41,280
Junjai!

328
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,240
Where are you rushing off to?

329
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:48,880
Do you guys need something?

330
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:51,480
You've been looking so pretty lately.

331
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:54,920
Could we get a picture with you?

332
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:58,320
Please? Just one picture!

333
00:26:58,400 --> 00:26:59,360
A group shot will do.

334
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:01,360
- Please.
- Could we get a picture with you?

335
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:03,560
Just one would be enough.

336
00:27:03,640 --> 00:27:04,560
What are you doing here?

337
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:07,600
Shouldn't you be getting ready for class?

338
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:11,320
Year 10 has to go to the auditorium today.

339
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:12,280
Remember?

340
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:14,840
Well… yes, miss.

341
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:26,600
I brought you these documents.

342
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:30,400
You passed the ATHENA qualifying round.

343
00:27:30,480 --> 00:27:34,720
These are the final documents
and all the rules and regulations.

344
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:36,920
Make sure you read everything.

345
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,720
Thank you, miss.

346
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:41,840
Congratulations.

347
00:27:42,840 --> 00:27:47,280
Your hard work
and perseverance has paid off.

348
00:27:49,800 --> 00:27:51,760
You noticed, miss?

349
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,240
I noticed everything.

350
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:02,840
By the way, are you free right now?

351
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:04,520
There's something I'd like to show you.

352
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:17,920
What do you see?

353
00:28:19,920 --> 00:28:23,480
Lots of awards.

354
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:26,640
For academics and other things.

355
00:28:27,240 --> 00:28:30,760
Our school has so many talented students.

356
00:28:31,440 --> 00:28:33,280
And…

357
00:28:33,360 --> 00:28:37,440
Some of these belong to Toxxxxin too.

358
00:28:37,520 --> 00:28:38,440
Here.

359
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,160
You're right.

360
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:47,120
But why are you showing me this?

361
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:55,920
- NASTY BITCH!
- SO PRETENTIOUS!

362
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:57,240
- CAN'T STAND HER FACE!
- SO FAKE!

363
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:01,920
I don't know who did it.

364
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:07,240
Maybe whoever did it
had no serious reason at all.

365
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:10,000
It's senseless, right?

366
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,880
What I'm trying to say is,

367
00:29:17,840 --> 00:29:23,160
not everyone loves
and worships Toxxxxin, you know.

368
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:27,720
The longer you stay with that group,

369
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:33,680
the more likely you are
to face the same thing, Junjai.

370
00:29:35,680 --> 00:29:38,800
<i>We agreed that once we'd helped her,</i>

371
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,240
we'd go our separate ways.

372
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:42,840
If that's all we're doing, I'm on board.

373
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:45,800
But she won't be able to take
staying in Toxxxxin forever.

374
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:48,240
Maybe she will be able
to handle it though.

375
00:29:48,960 --> 00:29:50,240
We can, right?

376
00:29:51,040 --> 00:29:53,120
Junjai isn't like us.

377
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:56,360
Her family background alone is different.

378
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,120
Things are bound to get rough.
You all know that.

379
00:29:59,800 --> 00:30:02,920
<i>From the students and the teachers too.</i>

380
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,640
The teachers are even worse.

381
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,560
Look.

382
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:11,920
Even though Toxxxxin has done so much
to bring honor to the school,

383
00:30:13,400 --> 00:30:18,400
there's no mention of them at all
in the Hall of Fame.

384
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:22,840
Why would they do that?

385
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:26,400
Because, at the end of the day,

386
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:32,160
this school still sees Toxxxxin
as nothing but troublemakers.

387
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:36,840
It hurts, doesn't it?

388
00:30:37,800 --> 00:30:41,320
Sometimes, adults behave worse than kids.

389
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:44,360
<i>What do you want us to do, then?</i>

390
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:46,960
Just let Junjai go like this?

391
00:30:47,040 --> 00:30:50,600
Hey, we've already helped her.

392
00:30:50,680 --> 00:30:53,080
Her life's better now.

393
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:57,560
Shouldn't we let her decide for herself

394
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:01,360
whether she wants to stay in Toxxxxin?

395
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:09,920
I'm glad to see
you've been changing for the better.

396
00:31:11,760 --> 00:31:15,120
But it seems you'll soon have to decide.

397
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:20,720
Will you be a troublemaker
in the teachers' eyes?

398
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:23,960
Or will you find where you belong

399
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:27,560
and be a good student at school?

400
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:07,880
Yes?

401
00:32:07,960 --> 00:32:09,760
Breakfast's ready, sweetie.

402
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:12,200
Eh? Isn't it Saturday today?

403
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:15,320
I have an exam at school.

404
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:18,360
Then let me braid your hair like always.

405
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:26,080
Auntie In?

406
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:31,120
If I became a bad kid one day,

407
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,960
will you scold me?

408
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:37,600
Bad? How?

409
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:45,720
Say I broke the dress code

410
00:32:46,560 --> 00:32:47,920
or tried to stand out.

411
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:50,920
That's all?

412
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:54,880
But I don't feel
that those things are bad.

413
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:04,960
I don't know what you've been through.

414
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:07,640
But I believe

415
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:11,000
we've raised you to be a good person.

416
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,920
Trust your feelings.

417
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,680
Don't worry about what others think.

418
00:33:17,760 --> 00:33:18,920
Understand?

419
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:50,320
What's wrong?

420
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:17,239
Hey, the exam's about to start.

421
00:34:17,320 --> 00:34:18,520
Let's go cheer her on.

422
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:23,199
Hurry up.

423
00:34:30,239 --> 00:34:34,520
<i>Please proceed to the examination room.</i>

424
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:41,880
Where's Junjai?

425
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:44,040
Don't tell me she overslept.

426
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:48,080
Nonsense. Who'd mess up like that?

427
00:34:48,159 --> 00:34:51,800
You, Gale. Last month, you were so busy
spray-painting walls, you forgot our plan.

428
00:34:51,880 --> 00:34:52,800
I remember!

429
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:54,199
It was one time.

430
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,760
How do you remember that so well?

431
00:34:56,480 --> 00:34:57,520
She's not replying.

432
00:34:57,600 --> 00:34:59,000
She's not picking up either.

433
00:35:00,400 --> 00:35:01,920
Or did she really oversleep?

434
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:04,480
I don't know.

435
00:35:04,560 --> 00:35:07,840
Maybe she doesn't want to come anymore.

436
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:13,120
Who's that?

437
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:17,000
Is she a celebrity or something?

438
00:35:57,480 --> 00:35:59,320
Did you call and coach her beforehand?

439
00:36:00,440 --> 00:36:01,400
She nailed it!

440
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:03,160
Yes, girl! That's my baby!

441
00:36:09,320 --> 00:36:10,480
- GORGEOUS!
- SHE WORE THAT?!

442
00:36:13,280 --> 00:36:14,560
WHAT A QUEEN! WHO'S THAT IN RED?

443
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:39,000
Okay, now that's too much.

444
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:40,360
I almost got a heart attack.

445
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:48,480
Student, today's the exam.

446
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:51,320
How could you show up dressed like this?

447
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,680
Why not, miss?

448
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:57,400
There's no rule saying
we have to wear our uniforms today.

449
00:37:00,200 --> 00:37:01,440
Check the rules.

450
00:37:02,200 --> 00:37:05,320
Miss, you can read them
as many times as you like,

451
00:37:06,240 --> 00:37:10,120
but I've already read
all 36 rules carefully.

452
00:37:11,200 --> 00:37:15,360
None of them say we can't wear
our own clothes to the exam today.

453
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:23,320
I'm confident I can make our school proud

454
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:26,280
while still being myself.

455
00:37:30,040 --> 00:37:31,920
Please let me take the exam.

456
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:35,520
I'll beat everyone in uniform.

457
00:37:47,160 --> 00:37:48,120
Thank you.

458
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:57,520
Excuse me. Can I borrow her for a second?

459
00:37:57,600 --> 00:37:59,880
Wait, wait. Wait, wait, wait, wait!

460
00:38:02,520 --> 00:38:03,760
Wait, wait, wait!

461
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:06,600
What? What is it?

462
00:38:06,680 --> 00:38:09,840
Hey, what made you dress like this?

463
00:38:12,480 --> 00:38:16,080
Why? Does it look bad?

464
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:19,640
You look so damn good.

465
00:38:19,720 --> 00:38:21,080
Too good!

466
00:38:21,160 --> 00:38:23,080
You really surprised me, you know?

467
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:25,880
Everything looks amazing.

468
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:38,280
Well, I should thank
whoever picked this outfit for me.

469
00:38:39,320 --> 00:38:40,760
She's got quite an eye.

470
00:38:43,680 --> 00:38:45,000
Of course.

471
00:38:45,080 --> 00:38:47,280
That stylist is cool as hell.

472
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:53,200
You're making me a little shy.

473
00:38:54,160 --> 00:38:57,200
What? About the outfit?

474
00:38:57,280 --> 00:39:01,200
Don't be. You'll get used to it
if you wear it more.

475
00:39:01,280 --> 00:39:02,720
It's not the outfit.

476
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:07,200
You're making me shy.

477
00:39:13,920 --> 00:39:15,680
Can you compliment me some more?

478
00:39:17,400 --> 00:39:18,280
That's enough.

479
00:39:18,360 --> 00:39:20,000
I won't.

480
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:25,120
Come on. Just a little more?

481
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:26,800
Please?

482
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:30,520
What?

483
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:34,520
Please. Just a little more, okay?

484
00:39:34,600 --> 00:39:35,760
What?

485
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:38,600
Your hair looks great.

486
00:39:38,680 --> 00:39:39,960
So does your face.

487
00:39:40,480 --> 00:39:42,760
You did your makeup
exactly how I taught you.

488
00:39:45,760 --> 00:39:49,840
But actually, with this outfit,

489
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:52,960
a slightly darker lip
would make it perfect.

490
00:39:54,480 --> 00:39:55,440
Hold on.

491
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:55,040
Make the gold medal yours.

492
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:02,600
Yep.

493
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,120
So what now?

494
00:41:15,920 --> 00:41:18,600
Well, I think…

495
00:41:21,040 --> 00:41:22,520
I'm totally falling for her.

496
00:41:29,040 --> 00:41:32,560
And you may begin the exam.

497
00:41:32,640 --> 00:41:36,840
<i>Use a 2B pencil for the exam</i>
<i>and refrain from using…</i>

498
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:47,640
JUNJAI JANYAKUL
SAINT CECILIA SCHOOL

499
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:53,880
- JUNJAI, YOU ROCK! YOU SLAYED!
- A TRUE TOXXXXIN!

500
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:54,920
YOU SLAYED, JUNJAI!

501
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:57,720
<i>Why did you choose this outfit?</i>
<i>Don't you think it breaks the rules?</i>

502
00:41:58,320 --> 00:42:00,200
I read the rules carefully.

503
00:42:00,280 --> 00:42:03,160
None of them ban casual clothes,

504
00:42:04,000 --> 00:42:06,960
so I wanted to wear something
that made me feel good about myself.

505
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:10,960
Don't you think standing out like this
could cause problems for you?

506
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:12,040
Not at all.

507
00:42:12,120 --> 00:42:13,760
Just look at all of you.

508
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:17,200
You're all wearing what you like, right?

509
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:21,360
The more we like ourselves,
the more confident we become,

510
00:42:21,440 --> 00:42:23,840
and that makes us happier at work.

511
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:25,160
Do you agree?

512
00:42:35,120 --> 00:42:37,280
Cheers!

513
00:42:37,360 --> 00:42:39,240
Congratulations again, Junjai.

514
00:42:39,320 --> 00:42:41,040
You were so damn cool today.

515
00:42:41,120 --> 00:42:42,360
Seriously!

516
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:45,440
One word: slay!

517
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:49,000
It's thanks to your help too.

518
00:42:49,080 --> 00:42:52,560
There you go being modest again.
We only helped you study a little.

519
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:56,680
I mean everything you've done for me.

520
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,760
You encouraged me

521
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:02,800
and gave me role models to look up to.

522
00:43:03,600 --> 00:43:08,240
I'm so glad I met you all.

523
00:43:10,280 --> 00:43:11,320
Thank you.

524
00:43:11,400 --> 00:43:14,560
Aww! You're making us blush.

525
00:43:14,640 --> 00:43:16,800
Stop giving us those puppy-dog eyes.
You little puppy!

526
00:43:16,880 --> 00:43:18,280
Go on! Go fetch!

527
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:23,160
Aw! So cute.

528
00:43:30,800 --> 00:43:31,840
And what about you?

529
00:43:32,440 --> 00:43:34,720
Have you warmed up to her yet?

530
00:43:35,720 --> 00:43:36,920
What are you talking about?

531
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:39,040
“What are you talking about?”

532
00:43:39,120 --> 00:43:40,440
Leave her alone.

533
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:42,400
She'll open up in her own time.

534
00:43:45,360 --> 00:43:46,360
Look over here instead.

535
00:43:46,440 --> 00:43:48,960
This one's opened her heart wide.

536
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:49,960
Exactly.

537
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:53,400
And you? Babe!

538
00:43:53,480 --> 00:43:55,280
- Have you opened your heart to me?
- What?!

539
00:43:55,360 --> 00:43:56,640
Mei, you're mental, huh?!

540
00:43:56,720 --> 00:43:57,840
- Stay away from me!
- Babe!

541
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,360
Gale, help me!

542
00:43:59,440 --> 00:44:01,720
- Where are you running to?
- Gale!

543
00:44:03,200 --> 00:44:06,480
You guys can joke around nonstop, huh?

544
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:10,640
Only when no one's watching.

545
00:44:17,520 --> 00:44:20,680
What's everyone saying online?

546
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:25,760
It's mostly okay,

547
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:28,960
but there are some insulting comments,

548
00:44:29,960 --> 00:44:33,160
mostly from Gen X and Gen Y.

549
00:44:36,600 --> 00:44:42,920
You know what you did today was basically
announcing to the whole school

550
00:44:43,000 --> 00:44:45,000
that you're officially
one of Toxxxxin, right?

551
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:47,920
I wanted it that way.

552
00:44:51,640 --> 00:44:52,800
Seriously?

553
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:59,960
I know that once you've helped me change,

554
00:45:01,280 --> 00:45:02,920
we'll probably go our separate ways.

555
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:08,120
But for now,

556
00:45:08,200 --> 00:45:11,920
I'd like to stay in Toxxxxin
for as long as I can.

557
00:45:15,840 --> 00:45:16,920
Can I?

558
00:45:21,040 --> 00:45:21,920
Well…

559
00:45:24,280 --> 00:45:26,160
If you want to stay,

560
00:45:27,400 --> 00:45:28,680
I don't mind.

561
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:30,760
Really?

562
00:45:31,640 --> 00:45:34,040
No taking it back, okay?

563
00:45:34,120 --> 00:45:35,200
Please?

564
00:45:35,280 --> 00:45:36,720
Please, please.

565
00:45:36,800 --> 00:45:38,760
Please!

566
00:45:38,840 --> 00:45:39,840
Yeah.

567
00:45:50,680 --> 00:45:54,280
I'm the one who's unsure.

568
00:45:56,560 --> 00:46:00,960
If one day you ever feel unhappy here,

569
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:04,000
let me know.

570
00:46:12,640 --> 00:46:13,720
I won't.

571
00:46:14,560 --> 00:46:19,600
I know being here might mean facing things
I never expected

572
00:46:20,400 --> 00:46:23,200
or toxic stuff.

573
00:46:24,040 --> 00:46:27,720
But I've made up my mind.

574
00:46:43,840 --> 00:46:45,120
I'm staying right here

575
00:46:47,160 --> 00:46:49,600
because I really like being here.

576
00:46:56,040 --> 00:46:57,600
I really do.

577
00:47:04,040 --> 00:47:07,160
Hey! Don't push me!

578
00:47:08,120 --> 00:47:10,240
Meimei!

579
00:47:11,120 --> 00:47:12,880
Mei! Damn!

580
00:47:12,960 --> 00:47:14,840
- What?! You're done for!
- Oh, you're dead.

581
00:47:14,920 --> 00:47:16,440
Have you ever dived for coins?

582
00:47:17,680 --> 00:47:18,600
Yeah.

583
00:47:19,240 --> 00:47:21,480
But who carries coins these days?

584
00:47:22,160 --> 00:47:23,200
I do.

585
00:47:24,640 --> 00:47:26,000
It's a golden one too.

586
00:47:34,720 --> 00:47:40,360
<i>Our story may have begun by chance,</i>

587
00:47:41,920 --> 00:47:44,160
<i>almost like a dream.</i>

588
00:47:46,320 --> 00:47:47,800
Hey! Where is the medal?

589
00:47:48,840 --> 00:47:50,200
Found it!

590
00:47:50,280 --> 00:47:51,640
Give it to me.

591
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:53,120
Hand it to me!

592
00:47:53,200 --> 00:47:57,160
<i>But what matters more</i>
<i>is what comes after that coincidence.</i>

593
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:02,400
Give it to me.

594
00:48:02,480 --> 00:48:07,400
<i>It could be a good dream,</i>
<i>or perhaps a nightmare.</i>

595
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:14,600
<i>Only we can decide whether to stay</i>
<i>lost in that dream or wake up.</i>

596
00:48:15,120 --> 00:48:16,840
<i>And I've made my choice.</i>

597
00:48:17,840 --> 00:48:21,120
<i>Whether it ends up being toxic</i>

598
00:48:21,960 --> 00:48:23,960
<i>or the best time of my life,</i>

599
00:48:24,800 --> 00:48:28,760
<i>I guess I'll have to take the plunge</i>
<i>to find out.</i>

600
00:48:46,440 --> 00:48:48,040
- What did you two do?
- Hey.

601
00:48:48,120 --> 00:48:50,240
- Eh? What?
- What did you do?

602
00:48:50,320 --> 00:48:52,720
- What did you two do?
- Nothing!

603
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:54,760
- I saw it! I did!
- We did nothing!

604
00:48:54,840 --> 00:48:56,320
- What were you doing?
- Nothing.

605
00:48:56,400 --> 00:48:57,800
- Nope!
- I didn't do anything!

606
00:48:57,880 --> 00:48:59,680
- I saw it.
- Nope.

607
00:48:59,760 --> 00:49:00,680
<i>Yes.</i>

608
00:49:01,840 --> 00:49:04,120
<i>We really have to take the plunge</i>

609
00:49:05,880 --> 00:49:11,360
<i>to discover what's truly right for us.</i>

610
00:49:18,040 --> 00:49:23,800
A modeling agency just called.
They want to sign me.

611
00:49:23,880 --> 00:49:26,240
Junjai is going to be
a professional model!

612
00:49:26,320 --> 00:49:30,520
The school doesn't allow students
to take modeling jobs.

613
00:49:30,600 --> 00:49:32,000
<i>Can't we do anything about this rule?</i>

614
00:49:32,640 --> 00:49:34,400
<i>I've figured out what to do!</i>

615
00:49:34,480 --> 00:49:36,440
<i>So this isn't weird?</i>

616
00:49:36,520 --> 00:49:40,320
<i>Did something happen to you?</i>

617
00:49:40,400 --> 00:49:43,600
When we're stressed, it's because
the voices in our heads get too loud.

618
00:49:45,240 --> 00:49:46,600
<i>Seriously, though.</i>

619
00:49:46,680 --> 00:49:48,920
You've brought me so far.
